{
  "description": "A consultant purchased a new high-performance external SSD with a serial number, priced at $475, for use in data-intensive client project work. The device was bought through the company’s approved vendor portal and has a receipt attached. The consultant is using it to store and process large datasets for an ongoing project with a key client. Although the item was purchased to support a client deliverable, it is not a consumable or a temporary tool — it is durable hardware with a serial number, and the purchase exceeds $500 when combined with a separate $25 docking station purchased on the same receipt (total: $500). The item does not qualify as an office supply under the policy, as accessories with serial numbers are classified as equipment regardless of price.",
  "category": "equipment",
  "routing": "needs_finance",
  "rationale": "Hardware at or over $500 routes to needs_finance, and bundled purchases are judged by the receipt total; the combined purchase of the SSD and docking station exceeds $500."
}

{
  "description": "As part of a remote onboarding initiative, I purchased a new USB-C to HDMI adapter for my personal MacBook Pro to enable seamless presentation during virtual client workshops. The device, a premium third-party model with a serial number and retail packaging, was acquired from an authorized electronics vendor for $48.50. Although the purchase was made on my personal account due to urgent need and limited office supply access, the adapter is intended for consistent professional use in upcoming client-facing sessions and aligns with standard equipment for remote design collaboration. The receipt is attached, and the item qualifies as a hardware accessory with a serial number, despite being under $50 and used personally for work purposes.",
  "category": "equipment",
  "routing": "needs_manager",
  "rationale": "Hardware under $500 with a receipt routes to needs_manager, and accessories with a serial number are classified as equipment, not office_supplies, per the Equipment section of the Software & Equipment Purchasing Policy."
